  "id": "COMPOUND:42490 - PROTEIN:4961",
  "verbalization": "Ascidiathiazone B is implicated in the biological activity of FaDu through a series of target relationships, all centered on the Dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinase. This kinase is a common target for multiple compounds, including Ascidiathiazone B, which is shown to interact with it directly. The evidence suggests that Ascidiathiazone B may act through a shared mechanism, targeting this kinase, and that this kinase is ultimately a target of several other compounds, including 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine and Javanicoside F, which also lead to FaDu. The integration of these pathways implies that Ascidiathiazone B may exert its effects by modulating the activity of this kinase, potentially influencing cellular processes in FaDu cells. The consistent targeting of this kinase across different compounds supports the hypothesis that Ascidiathiazone B interacts with FaDu via a mechanism involving this kinase, though the exact molecular pathway remains to be fully elucidated.",
